# Frontend UI guardrails

- In a project that uses `@astryxdesign/core`, or a new React UI with no design system, build with Astryx. Do not mix Astryx into a project that standardizes on another design system unless the user asks for a migration.
- Look up components with the `astryx` MCP (`search`, then `get`) or the project's `astryx` CLI before using them. Do not invent props or import paths.
- Start new pages from the template `astryx build "<idea>"` names; keep its frame, gap, and padding.
- Use components instead of raw `<div>`/`<span>` for layout, and tokens instead of hardcoded hex/px, `style={{…}}`, ad-hoc CSS, or `:root` overrides.
- Prefer structural fixes (template frame, parent stack, component props) over one-off offsets or selector overrides. Avoid `!important` and arbitrary z-index escalation.
- Before finishing, re-read changed files and replace leftover raw elements or hardcoded values with components or tokens.

Use the `frontend-ui-development` skill for the full workflow, adoption steps, and phase-specific guidance.
